Detach the box subtree of a box that leaves the box tree; rebuild it in full when it
returns (Roves; same defect as Blitz #1577).

Base: crates.io blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.4 (DioxusLabs/blitz
92b11f1bd8ab7975411328b0406a95a09445b4e7, packages/blitz-dom), after 0001-0004.
Applied in support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-dom; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.

resolve_layout_children only visits boxes reachable from the root. A box dropped from
its container's rebuilt list (display:none ancestor, detached from the DOM, now inline
content of an inline root) kept its layout_children; freeing one of its children left a
freed key there and the debug assertion assert_layout_parents_consistent aborted the
next resolve ("layout child NodeId(..) of NodeId(..) is not in the slab"). Before a
rebuild the container records its previous boxes (also those inside the anonymous
blocks it frees) with layout_parent cleared; afterwards every previous box that was not
adopted is detached (child lists taken, links cleared, anonymous blocks freed). A box
without layout_children is rebuilt with ALL_DAMAGE, an invalidated layout cache and
marked damaged-descendant flags. The assertion and the other resolver paths are
unchanged; no kept list is filtered.

